  "analysis": {
    "primary_estimand": "At the final checkpoint, average nDCG@10 over the four predeclared learning rates within optimizer for each task, then contrast Muon-AdamW, NorMuon-AdamW, and NorMuon-Muon across the 14 paired tasks.",
    "primary_support_rule": "An optimizer-family advantage is supported only when its simultaneous 95% interval versus AdamW lies wholly above zero and all four rates completed. An interval wholly below zero supports a disadvantage; otherwise report inconclusive.",
    "primary_uncertainty": "50,000 paired task bootstraps with seed 20260903; simultaneous max-T 95% intervals over the three optimizer contrasts.",
    "secondary_estimand": "Compare the validation-selected recipe per optimizer on final-checkpoint mean nDCG@10 using the same paired max-T procedure; label this secondary.",
    "stability": "Report completion, non-finite values, gradient norms, peak memory, accepted wall time, checkpoint bytes, and optimizer-state bytes for every run.",
    "training_dynamics": "Report every optimizer-rate-task checkpoint, optimizer-level stage means, and trapezoidal area over normalized progress. Dynamics are descriptive unless an interval procedure is explicitly added without changing the primary rule.",
    "weight_space": "At all five checkpoints, report update norm, update-to-weight ratio, singular-value effective/stable rank, top-subspace overlap with AdamW, and representation/retrieval bridges. These mechanism analyses are secondary and cannot substitute for the primary retrieval contrast."
  },
